  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 accuracy. We know multiprofile+avgpool is a strong combination (+10.6 pts over singleprofile), and avgpool beats transformer. In singleprofile, pca_n2000 (0.485) outperforms scgpt (0.411), but scvi_n200 has not yet been tested in any setting. Question: Does scvi_n200, a learned latent-space encoder, improve on pca_n2000 in the multiprofile+avgpool setting where we've already seen the largest gains? This is a single-variable swap (encoder only) from our best config, cleanly isolating the representation effect. Why this is the best use of experiment 6: With 4 experiments remaining, we need to determine whether a better RNA encoder exists before committing budget to multimodal fusion (which currently rests on a very weak image signal at 0.208). If scvi_n200 improves on 0.591, it reshapes the multimodal strategy; if not, we confirm pca_n2000 as optimal and can pivot remaining experiments to testing whether multimodal fusion or a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) adds value on top of the best RNA baseline."
}

